WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.169 --> 00:00:11.150
&gt;&gt;

00:00:11.169 --> 00:00:13.150
[introductory music]

00:00:13.169 --> 00:00:14.150
&gt;&gt;

00:00:14.169 --> 00:00:15.169
[pause]

00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:17.920
MC Hammer: Would you mind just for a second if everybody

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.070
would just stand up and kind of shake it out a little bit?

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:27.539
It's been about thirty minutes.

00:00:27.559 --> 00:00:31.009
You might say hello to the person next to you, shake their

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:32.030
hand, you know?

00:00:31.779 --> 00:00:32.780
[laughter]

00:00:31.779 --> 00:00:33.030
&gt;&gt; Hey, microwave before. Hammer, starts.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:46.979
There is a word of mouth on Twitter that you should write a

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.000
ten tweet vis.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.000
[laughter]

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:59.139
MC Hammer: All right.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:00.159
[laughter]

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:00.909
Thanks for having us here this morning.

00:01:00.909 --> 00:01:09.959
I always consider it an equal exchange to interact with

00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:10.979
fervent minds.

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:15.230
So with minds that are fertile ground -- entrepreneurs, been

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:19.570
an entrepreneur -- I shouldn't frame it like this, but I

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.900
will -- "before you were born."

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:22.920
[laughter]

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.170
I've been an entrepreneur.

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:26.409
My first job was when I was eight years old.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.250
And I started with the Oakland A's when I was nine years

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:29.560
old.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.560
I was around a very innovative owner in baseball who thought

00:01:32.579 --> 00:01:33.579
baseball was boring.

00:01:33.579 --> 00:01:37.629
He thought the game was so boring that even he had a rabbit

00:01:37.649 --> 00:01:42.290
pop out the ground and hand the umpire the baseballs instead

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.450
of just the traditional "get it out of the bucket," he

00:01:45.469 --> 00:01:48.219
thought that -- he was so stubborn as an owner -- that it

00:01:48.219 --> 00:01:51.219
would be good that a mule would be his mascot, and he

00:01:51.219 --> 00:01:53.469
brought the mule into the hotel during baseball league

00:01:53.469 --> 00:01:54.670
meetings.

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:58.920
He took the game of baseball from traditional uniforms to

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:00.280
colored uniforms.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:02.539
He innovated the designated hitter.

00:02:02.559 --> 00:02:06.409
He hired track stars for the playoffs in the World Series --

00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:09.680
go right over to Cal Berkeley and take a track star and pay

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.680
him a hundred thousand dollars just so "In case we made the

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.680
World Series and we need to steal second base, he didn't

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:18.180
even have to know how to play baseball, just steal second

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:18.430
base."

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.430
[Laughter]

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:23.119
So I've been around innovators and innovation all my life.

00:02:23.139 --> 00:02:27.879
I'm very -- a serial entrepreneur, and I understand the

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.499
mindset of an entrepreneur.

00:02:30.519 --> 00:02:35.019
And so, I'll try to make this as valuable as I can from that

00:02:35.039 --> 00:02:40.359
standpoint, and also from the standpoint of social media --

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:43.709
and, in particular, social media optimization vs. search

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:46.469
engine optimization.

00:02:46.489 --> 00:02:52.879
Just real quick -- over the surface and 30,000 foot view --

00:02:52.900 --> 00:03:01.219
earlier I put up "See Her Face", which was like, 'What is

00:03:01.239 --> 00:03:04.249
that?' right?

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:08.749
Because of social media, it is so much easier -- the bar of

00:03:08.769 --> 00:03:11.149
entering -- this is strictly for entrepreneurs and thinking

00:03:11.169 --> 00:03:12.929
of starting businesses.

00:03:12.949 --> 00:03:16.789
The old model of having to raise x amount of dollars of

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:17.810
angel capital.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:21.039
And then, you know, get ready for your VC Round.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:24.799
Before you even get there today, you can use all of these

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:27.319
social media tools to see if you really have something,

00:03:26.569 --> 00:03:27.569
right?

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:29.959
And insert yourself into the conversation.

00:03:29.979 --> 00:03:32.349
So why did I choose this?

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:36.120
I have a song on a project that I'm working on, and it's

00:03:35.549 --> 00:03:37.279
called "See Her Face."

00:03:37.299 --> 00:03:40.299
When I finished the song, I said, "Woe, See Her Face, okay."

00:03:40.189 --> 00:03:47.819
I made a big dance, party record that was optimized for an

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.189
audience that may also love fashion.

00:03:51.209 --> 00:03:55.769
So rather than waiting until after the song has received a

00:03:55.789 --> 00:03:58.599
certain amount of gross impressions and other media around

00:03:58.619 --> 00:04:02.899
it, I decided to create the media myself and insert myself

00:04:02.919 --> 00:04:06.599
into the fashion world without spending a dollar.

00:04:06.619 --> 00:04:10.979
And why not shoot for the top since other people now pay for

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.000
the content?

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.250
In other words, for me to source a content that I needed for

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:19.189
my launch into the fashion world, all I had to do was go to

00:04:19.209 --> 00:04:20.209
YouTube.

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:21.670
It didn't take long.

00:04:21.689 --> 00:04:24.439
I didn't have to go out and shoot the video.

00:04:24.189 --> 00:04:26.939
I didn't have to cut the deal with the models.

00:04:26.689 --> 00:04:28.939
I didn't have to do any of that.

00:04:28.689 --> 00:04:32.900
At the same time, I'm making it aware to D&amp;G, Versace -- if

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:37.569
we go down the page, you'll see Prada -- that I'm going to

00:04:37.589 --> 00:04:41.829
make available not only the events, the songs, and the

00:04:41.849 --> 00:04:45.829
social media campaign for these brands, but I'm going to

00:04:45.849 --> 00:04:49.269
create a destination that they can go to around an actual

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.480
brand: See Her Face.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:54.840
Because obviously, although it's superficial, models start

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.810
with the outer appearance and then -- well, I guess in

00:04:57.829 --> 00:05:00.329
models, we don't ever get into necessarily the depth.

00:05:00.129 --> 00:05:01.129
[Laughter]

00:05:00.129 --> 00:05:08.350
But, that's not to say it's not any substance there,

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.370
[laughter], but we have to be real, right?

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.579
So initially, we start with the outer appearance.

00:05:12.599 --> 00:05:16.139
And then, they clothe them in all these great designs.

00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:18.910
Later on -- for a lot of you who are fashion oriented --

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.930
take a look at what's on there.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.930
And this is all 2010 stuff, so you'll see the spring and

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:26.680
summer collections, but the point that I'm making is, as an

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:29.589
entrepreneur -- and this being Entrepreneur Week -- and

00:05:29.609 --> 00:05:34.199
focusing on the tools of social media, it took me at -- I

00:05:34.219 --> 00:05:36.089
think I used -- yeah, I used blogspot.

00:05:36.109 --> 00:05:38.609
I shouldn't even say, "I think I used blogspot."

00:05:38.359 --> 00:05:40.670
I used blogspot for a very particular reason.

00:05:40.689 --> 00:05:44.480
I found out that, within the Google search engine, when you

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.910
use blogspot, it's optimized.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:49.430
So in the search return, it comes to the top.

00:05:49.279 --> 00:05:51.279
So it wasn't an accident. And so --

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:53.430
Audience member: Why do you think I'm on buzz?

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.930
MC Hammer: Is that why you're --?

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:55.680
[laughter]

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.680
It's very important. It's very important.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:06:00.050
And so, if you look -- and, by the way, the Twitter

00:06:00.069 --> 00:06:01.470
optimization works the same way.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:05.350
So if you look on Twitter -- for those of you on it right

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:09.730
now -- and if you Twitter Blast24, you'll see a lot of MC

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:13.189
Hammer come up around Blast24, but what is that?

00:06:13.209 --> 00:06:15.959
Well, what I'm doing is, I'm doing two things.

00:06:15.459 --> 00:06:17.459
I've already began to seed the content.

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:20.279
The content was sourced, again, from places like YouTube and

00:06:20.299 --> 00:06:21.299
other places with video.

00:06:21.299 --> 00:06:24.970
Ultimately, I want to build a destination for citizen

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:26.350
journalism.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.579
We were talking about "social good" earlier.

00:06:28.599 --> 00:06:33.019
Now, this is another startup I'm doing, but I'm not doing it

00:06:33.039 --> 00:06:34.199
with the traditional model.

00:06:34.219 --> 00:06:37.189
These tools have lowered the bar of entry.

00:06:37.209 --> 00:06:42.189
And the bar of entry now is here.

00:06:42.209 --> 00:06:45.220
It's really in how active you are.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:49.850
Earlier, I heard the dean say that -- it reminded me a lot

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.120
of a music conference I was at a couple weeks ago at the

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:53.370
Grammies.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:56.370
It said, you know, social media and all these new tools are

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.120
not the end-all.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.620
They're not going to supplement -- and, as a generalized

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:03.040
corporate statement, it's very true, but on many levels, I

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:06.629
would challenge you on that, because a lot of things are

00:07:06.649 --> 00:07:10.779
going to be replaced because of the realtime access of these

00:07:10.799 --> 00:07:11.799
platforms.

00:07:11.799 --> 00:07:15.549
And we don't even have time to go and pick up, per se, a

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:19.199
newspaper when I can just whip out my iPhone or my Android

00:07:19.219 --> 00:07:21.719
platform and go boom, boom, and it's right there.

00:07:21.579 --> 00:07:25.709
So, who's going to provide that information to me --

00:07:25.729 --> 00:07:29.680
recommendation is going to go further beyond the

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:32.199
traditional, "here's the paper, and here's the headlines."

00:07:31.799 --> 00:07:34.799
I want to know what you're reading, which is why trending

00:07:34.549 --> 00:07:37.170
topics are so popular, follow lists, and so forth.

00:07:37.189 --> 00:07:42.860
So, what I'm encouraging all you entrepreneurs in the room -

00:07:42.879 --> 00:07:46.639
- and I'm like Lloyd earlier -- when only half the room

00:07:46.659 --> 00:07:49.990
raise their hand on entrepreneurship, I'm always taken

00:07:50.009 --> 00:07:56.730
aback, because to have the opportunity in this model.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:08:00.879
This is the greatest opportunity ever to be an entrepreneur

00:08:00.899 --> 00:08:02.579
-- this time, right now.

00:08:02.599 --> 00:08:06.699
The down economy actually works in your favor.

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:09.209
Whenever a company like Intel.

00:08:09.229 --> 00:08:10.979
I was at the Intel CEO 600.

00:08:10.979 --> 00:08:13.229
I did the keynote for them two years ago.

00:08:12.589 --> 00:08:14.089
But this year, I was there.

00:08:14.089 --> 00:08:18.060
One of the things that they do as a company during a down

00:08:18.079 --> 00:08:21.430
market is, they double up on all of their investments and

00:08:21.449 --> 00:08:22.449
all of their bets.

00:08:22.449 --> 00:08:24.370
They double down in a down market.

00:08:24.389 --> 00:08:27.670
So in a down market, there's a great opportunity.

00:08:27.689 --> 00:08:29.899
One of the things that I love doing.

00:08:29.919 --> 00:08:32.669
I said this earlier -- I'm going to extend the conversation.

00:08:32.259 --> 00:08:35.740
I like working with great companies, and I like working with

00:08:35.759 --> 00:08:37.399
distressed companies.

00:08:37.419 --> 00:08:41.350
The distressed companies who need social media to tell their

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:49.100
story, to regain ground, and to communicate their message.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:52.250
There's a great opportunity in that, because as you can see

00:08:52.269 --> 00:08:55.429
from the FCC across the board, there's always a problem.

00:08:55.449 --> 00:08:58.610
There's always lawsuits. There's always challenges.

00:08:58.629 --> 00:09:01.379
And the other side of the story needs to be told.

00:09:01.169 --> 00:09:02.669
So there's three sides, right?

00:09:02.419 --> 00:09:04.830
Your side, their side, and the truth.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:05.850
[laughter]

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:11.009
Well, if you are actually telling the story yourself, the

00:09:11.029 --> 00:09:14.490
transparency -- is what you spoke of earlier.

00:09:14.509 --> 00:09:20.240
The transparency -- it distinguishes the initial effect of

00:09:20.259 --> 00:09:21.259
breaking news.

00:09:21.259 --> 00:09:25.809
So, I'll take David Letterman instead of Tiger Woods,

00:09:25.829 --> 00:09:27.330
because I know Tiger better.

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:28.350
[laughter]

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:36.679
It's not that complicated. Tiger is a friend.

00:09:36.699 --> 00:09:37.699
[laughter]

00:09:37.699 --> 00:09:43.259
Tiger is a friend. Tiger is a friend, and David is somebody

00:09:43.279 --> 00:09:46.779
I might turn up on once every five or six or seven or eight

00:09:46.389 --> 00:09:47.389
years.

00:09:47.389 --> 00:09:51.129
So, with that being said, David Letterman used the

00:09:51.149 --> 00:09:54.039
principles of social media to deal with his story.

00:09:54.059 --> 00:09:56.259
How many remember?

00:09:56.279 --> 00:10:00.379
He went out front and broke the story the night before to

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:03.360
the extent that his audience didn't even think it was

00:10:03.379 --> 00:10:04.379
serious.

00:10:04.379 --> 00:10:05.840
They laughed. They actually laughed.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:10.200
He said, "You know I've been couple things that

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:18.240
[laughter] you know, kind of, you know, feel the women

00:10:18.259 --> 00:10:19.259
around here.

00:10:19.259 --> 00:10:22.259
They say they're going to extort me because they know what

00:10:22.169 --> 00:10:23.169
I've been doing.

00:10:23.169 --> 00:10:24.919
And I just want to say that --"

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.639
Whatever, however he framed it, he told the story.

00:10:27.659 --> 00:10:28.909
Well, what did he do?

00:10:28.799 --> 00:10:32.319
Well, CNN can no longer now say, "breaking news."

00:10:32.339 --> 00:10:34.289
David told the story last night.

00:10:34.309 --> 00:10:38.710
So, what he did was get ahead of the story using the

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:40.049
principles of social media.

00:10:40.069 --> 00:10:43.419
That's a very social-media-oriented principle.

00:10:43.439 --> 00:10:47.939
So, if you utilize these tools and you entrepreneurs think

00:10:47.959 --> 00:10:52.779
about creating businesses around companies who need to tell

00:10:52.799 --> 00:10:56.740
stories -- who need a third voice to tell the story outside

00:10:56.759 --> 00:10:59.069
of themselves -- that is a huge market.

00:10:59.089 --> 00:11:03.350
It is the equivalent of being -- without being, right?

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.970
It's the equivalent of being a lawyer.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:09.610
Lawyers -- you don't necessarily get a lawyer because he's

00:11:09.629 --> 00:11:11.529
some expert.

00:11:11.549 --> 00:11:12.879
They admit it themselves.

00:11:12.899 --> 00:11:14.149
You know what they say?

00:11:13.879 --> 00:11:15.639
"I'm practicing law."

00:11:15.659 --> 00:11:16.659
[half-chuckle]

00:11:16.659 --> 00:11:20.169
They're practicing.

00:11:20.189 --> 00:11:21.189
[laughter]

00:11:21.189 --> 00:11:24.689
Some of this is going to -- You're going to win some; you're

00:11:24.339 --> 00:11:25.339
going to lose some.

00:11:25.339 --> 00:11:27.970
So, but --

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:29.240
[laughter] it happens every day.

00:11:29.209 --> 00:11:32.769
But if you can start to shape the story from your

00:11:32.789 --> 00:11:37.019
perspective, from the corporate perspective, tell the story.

00:11:37.039 --> 00:11:38.509
He mentioned Comcast earlier.

00:11:38.529 --> 00:11:42.149
Comcast, when they humanized themselves with social media,

00:11:42.169 --> 00:11:45.419
it's not that all of a sudden they became a perfect company,

00:11:45.169 --> 00:11:49.549
but what it did do was give you a voice, a ear to hear your

00:11:49.569 --> 00:11:50.569
problem.

00:11:50.569 --> 00:11:55.399
Nothing worse than "I'm trying to get this Mayweather fight"

00:11:55.419 --> 00:11:59.169
and I can't get it and all I'm getting is this voice thing

00:11:58.219 --> 00:11:59.219
over and over.

00:11:59.219 --> 00:12:00.490
That -- that really upsets me.

00:12:00.509 --> 00:12:03.929
But if I can tweet out and say, "Listen, man, now you guys

00:12:03.949 --> 00:12:05.990
knew this fight was coming four months ago."

00:12:06.009 --> 00:12:07.009
[laughter]

00:12:06.009 --> 00:12:11.000
"What do you mean you can't handle all the calls?"

00:12:11.019 --> 00:12:13.689
But isn't that how the company makes the money?

00:12:13.709 --> 00:12:18.100
Can you explain to me why my block cannot get through?

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:20.120
[imitating customer service guy] "Well, we didn't --"

00:12:19.039 --> 00:12:22.039
Okay, you didn't plan on it, but what's the resolution?

00:12:22.009 --> 00:12:24.759
I'm in a conflict resolution. How can you solve it?

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.600
His shirt says, "Smart is the new gangster."

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:27.250
I'm with that.

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:28.250
[laughter]

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:30.000
That's what his shirt says. "Smart is the new gangster."

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:36.250
Well, if smart is the new gangster, I need a gangster at

00:12:36.269 --> 00:12:39.069
Comcast right now

00:12:39.089 --> 00:12:45.639
[clapping] to tell me how we're going to solve this problem.

00:12:45.659 --> 00:12:49.309
Social media is not to be taken lightly.

00:12:49.329 --> 00:12:51.259
Don't let it be taken lightly.

00:12:51.279 --> 00:12:56.090
Don't be guilty of this great opportunity as entrepreneurs

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.659
right now.

00:12:57.679 --> 00:12:59.399
The gold strike earlier.

00:12:59.419 --> 00:13:03.350
The 1800's is back again, and you can either get left behind

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.730
by missing the mark.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:07.949
You think Pepsi shipped at $20 million over to social media

00:13:07.969 --> 00:13:10.370
just for the fun of it?

00:13:10.389 --> 00:13:12.939
Is that a nice number -- twenty million?

00:13:12.959 --> 00:13:15.720
Did that get anybody's attention, or did you continue with

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:18.399
the current project you were working on?

00:13:18.419 --> 00:13:22.919
See, as an entrepreneur, being able to shift -- to adapt --

00:13:22.939 --> 00:13:26.769
to the marketplace is very important no matter how much you

00:13:26.789 --> 00:13:29.529
loved your little idea.

00:13:29.549 --> 00:13:34.039
Sometimes you got to push that ideal aside and say, "It

00:13:34.059 --> 00:13:39.169
looks like here is the sweet spot." So, me? I know that the

00:13:39.189 --> 00:13:41.039
fashion companies are struggling because why?

00:13:41.059 --> 00:13:43.809
The economy is down; you're not spending as much money.

00:13:42.919 --> 00:13:43.919
Good. Hammertime.

00:13:43.919 --> 00:13:44.919
[laughter and clapping]

00:13:43.919 --> 00:13:44.919
Very good. Very good.

00:13:44.919 --> 00:13:56.740
That's when I hear, in the third person, "Hammertime."

00:13:56.759 --> 00:13:57.759
[laughter]

00:13:56.759 --> 00:14:02.529
I do, because I am used to engaging people and creating

00:14:02.549 --> 00:14:06.259
solutions and marketing and promotion and business.

00:14:06.279 --> 00:14:08.279
It's the foundation of the music industry.

00:14:08.259 --> 00:14:10.399
We go from grassroots to mainstream.

00:14:10.419 --> 00:14:11.669
That's what we do.

00:14:11.439 --> 00:14:14.139
We have an idea, a song. We conceive a song.

00:14:14.159 --> 00:14:16.159
At the time it's just a song.

00:14:15.529 --> 00:14:19.360
At a certain point -- as a writer myself -- I start to think

00:14:19.379 --> 00:14:21.629
the video by the second verse I'm writing.

00:14:21.379 --> 00:14:25.799
So I'm seeing the video in Madison Avenue that would be the

00:14:25.819 --> 00:14:26.819
commercial.

00:14:26.819 --> 00:14:28.679
So I see the commercial -- the trailer.

00:14:28.699 --> 00:14:31.949
Now, I'm starting to see, "Well, what are they going to wear

00:14:30.969 --> 00:14:31.969
doing?"

00:14:31.969 --> 00:14:33.719
All these things I could see initially.

00:14:33.719 --> 00:14:39.319
So, apply that to social media -- which my research for what

00:14:39.339 --> 00:14:42.639
I call "The Holy Grail of the Internet" at the time, in

00:14:42.659 --> 00:14:48.189
1995-96, that led me over -- I said this before -- to Apple,

00:14:48.209 --> 00:14:52.100
and I met a 14-year-old kid who was writing a code for

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.620
Quicktime who said he was going to solve my problem.

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.679
Back in -- about '96 that was.

00:14:56.699 --> 00:14:59.909
It was because I had a huge problem.

00:14:59.929 --> 00:15:04.389
There were two outlets for my art, and I didn't like that.

00:15:04.409 --> 00:15:05.439
Two outlets.

00:15:05.459 --> 00:15:09.169
That meant that 10 people could sit in a room and decide if

00:15:09.189 --> 00:15:12.389
my art is worthy for you to even view it.

00:15:12.409 --> 00:15:16.230
That is a barbaric thought.

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:18.250
[laughter and clapping] It was barbaric back then --

00:15:17.909 --> 00:15:19.159
Audience member: It certainly is.

00:15:19.159 --> 00:15:21.659
MC Hammer: -- and it was even -- and is even -- more

00:15:21.529 --> 00:15:22.529
barbaric today.

00:15:22.529 --> 00:15:24.029
You don't even think it.

00:15:23.459 --> 00:15:26.709
The first thing you want to do is post your video in the

00:15:26.709 --> 00:15:29.899
bathroom on YouTube to see if you can get a million views.

00:15:29.919 --> 00:15:32.980
We got people doing all kind of things. They jump off the

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.750
building with no parachute and land on their back for views,

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.000
right?

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.000
[laughter]

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.600
They're trying to get the most views.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:41.669
Well, here we have taken time to craft the product, market,

00:15:41.689 --> 00:15:43.970
mix, get it on the radio.

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:47.240
And then, you go, and you present it to this one guy, and

00:15:47.229 --> 00:15:51.720
his wife might have told him 'no' last night, and

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:54.490
[laughter] you know, you haven't been able, you know, they

00:15:54.069 --> 00:15:57.579
want four kids, and he only been able to make one.

00:15:57.599 --> 00:16:00.179
I don't know. He's mad today.

00:16:00.199 --> 00:16:03.610
And I come in with my happy video and thinking about some

00:16:03.629 --> 00:16:04.629
dance.

00:16:04.629 --> 00:16:07.379
[imitating the evaluator] "I don't like it. You should have

00:16:05.709 --> 00:16:06.709
put this in."

00:16:06.709 --> 00:16:11.129
Ho -- hold it. Who made you judge and jury?

00:16:11.149 --> 00:16:14.899
Are you telling me that, if you don't like it, I can't show

00:16:14.009 --> 00:16:15.009
it to the world?

00:16:15.009 --> 00:16:16.509
Well, we got to fix this.

00:16:16.509 --> 00:16:20.079
So, that is one of the reasons why I started searching for

00:16:20.099 --> 00:16:24.000
companies that would become -- later on -- YouTube.

00:16:24.019 --> 00:16:27.490
You know, it's all YouTube when I was there.

00:16:27.509 --> 00:16:30.259
When they had about four computers, but they were about the

00:16:30.039 --> 00:16:33.370
fourth or fifth company that I had went to over the years

00:16:33.389 --> 00:16:37.120
since '96 or '97 trying to find who would solve the three

00:16:37.139 --> 00:16:38.139
big problems.

00:16:38.139 --> 00:16:39.769
What were those three big challenges?

00:16:39.789 --> 00:16:41.299
One, compression technology.

00:16:41.319 --> 00:16:43.709
Two, broadband pipes.

00:16:43.729 --> 00:16:47.459
And last but not least -- and the most costly -- it was the

00:16:47.479 --> 00:16:48.799
last-mile solution.

00:16:48.819 --> 00:16:52.850
Who would pay to get the fiber from the curb to the

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:53.870
household?

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:57.889
Well, in searching that information and trying to find that

00:16:57.909 --> 00:17:00.799
out, it led me to places like YouTube down the road.

00:17:00.819 --> 00:17:05.149
So, because I was thinking of what I would be able to do and

00:17:05.169 --> 00:17:08.990
how I would monetize my content once I had control of it and

00:17:09.009 --> 00:17:12.740
had distribution, and able to market, I was able to make

00:17:12.759 --> 00:17:16.980
some good strategic partnerships, networking and friends in

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.250
the valley as a result of that going forward.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:23.690
So what I'm saying in a nutshell to all you entrepreneurs,

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:27.980
because I curtailed this for Entrepreneur Week -- I'm saying

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:31.490
that, Whatever it is that you're working on right now, use

00:17:31.509 --> 00:17:37.279
the tools of social media to keep your costs down, to do

00:17:37.299 --> 00:17:40.750
testing, to grab the analytics behind it and see what the

00:17:40.769 --> 00:17:42.920
people are saying.

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:46.670
Don't be afraid to curtail your ideal.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:48.190
I called it a "little ideal."

00:17:48.139 --> 00:17:50.889
Okay, I'm sorry. It's a big ideal.

00:17:50.909 --> 00:17:53.659
But whatever it is, little or big, if you're passionate

00:17:53.579 --> 00:17:57.349
about it, don't be afraid to utilize these tools to move it

00:17:57.369 --> 00:17:58.369
forward.

00:17:58.379 --> 00:18:02.099
Outside of this project, I have another project called "

00:18:02.119 --> 00:18:04.369
Hidden Knowledge" -- that knowledge is hidden, it's hidden

00:18:04.309 --> 00:18:07.629
to them that are lost -- which I deal with, again, social

00:18:07.649 --> 00:18:09.420
issues.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:13.490
I said earlier, but "social good" is also a business.

00:18:13.509 --> 00:18:16.609
And there are a lot of businesses that participate in social

00:18:16.629 --> 00:18:17.629
good.

00:18:17.629 --> 00:18:21.049
And finally again, I said the Blast24 -- another startup

00:18:21.069 --> 00:18:25.139
that I'm working on -- I'm utilizing the tools of social

00:18:25.159 --> 00:18:26.839
media to optimize.

00:18:26.859 --> 00:18:31.659
With that, I'll end, and we can go back to Step One for

00:18:31.679 --> 00:18:32.679
questions.

00:18:32.679 --> 00:18:35.929
And here's something very important that I'll say to you in

00:18:35.549 --> 00:18:36.740
ending.

00:18:36.759 --> 00:18:40.549
I meet a lot of people, very -- you would consider very --

00:18:40.569 --> 00:18:41.569
important people.

00:18:41.569 --> 00:18:45.569
I have an opportunity to exchange ideas with very important

00:18:45.589 --> 00:18:48.420
people who are very creative, whether it be the founders of

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:55.779
Google, Twitter, YouTube, Nancy Pelosi last week.

00:18:55.799 --> 00:18:56.799
People who --

00:18:56.799 --> 00:18:57.799
Audience member: Tiger Woods?

00:18:57.799 --> 00:19:01.460
MC Hammer: Tiger Woods.

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:02.730
[laughter] I'm never swayed.

00:19:02.599 --> 00:19:06.099
Again, I've been around -- as I'll just say this as we say "

00:19:04.289 --> 00:19:05.289
Tiger Woods."

00:19:05.289 --> 00:19:13.049
I've been around fame, fortune, people of means, since 1971.

00:19:13.069 --> 00:19:18.420
So just believe me when I tell you that I, as an individual

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:22.779
-- I'm still as proud of Tiger and what he's able to do in

00:19:22.799 --> 00:19:25.829
his profession as I was yesterday.

00:19:25.849 --> 00:19:30.309
If the cover is pulled off of every man -- we'll leave the

00:19:30.329 --> 00:19:32.329
women out of it.

00:19:32.349 --> 00:19:37.059
If the cover is pulled out off of every man and every man's

00:19:37.079 --> 00:19:42.319
personal life is exposed, what would you think of him?

00:19:42.339 --> 00:19:45.690
What would you think of your own life, if all of your quote

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:48.309
unquote "personal things" aren't covered?

00:19:48.329 --> 00:19:51.339
So just saying that, with Tiger Woods, I wish Tiger Woods

00:19:51.359 --> 00:19:56.069
the best on his road to recovery and that he continues to be

00:19:56.089 --> 00:19:57.769
a great athlete.

00:19:57.789 --> 00:20:00.190
And I'll end it right there.

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:00.410
&gt;&gt;

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.210
[Applause]

